tasks.detail:
Goal: Replace the monospace `pre-wrap` dump with the approved design — a header row (title, Copy, Expand/collapse) over a scroll area that renders the parsed prompt through `MarkdownBody`, every pi wrapper tag shown as a labelled section rule — and pin that rendered output with a component test in the same session.
Files: `components/SystemPromptPanel.tsx` (full rewrite of the existing 58-line file) and the new `components/SystemPromptPanel.test.mjs`. Do NOT touch `components/AppShell.tsx` — the call at `components/AppShell.tsx:2515-2519` (imported at `:17`) passes `loading`, `prompt`, `translate` and must keep working unchanged. Do not touch `lib/i18n/messages/*` (TASK-002 already landed the keys), `lib/system-prompt-markdown.ts` (TASK-001, merged and tested), `components/MarkdownBody.tsx`, `lib/markdown.ts`, `app/globals.css`, `demo/`, `docs/`, `eslint.config.mjs` or `.next-old-*`.

Contract — component module. Keep the existing public surface exactly:
  type Translate = (key: string, params?: Record<string, string | number>) => string;
  interface Props { loading: boolean; prompt: string | null; translate: Translate; }
  export function SystemPromptPanel({ loading, prompt, translate }: Props)
and additionally export the state-free view, following the repo's own precedent (`components/McpConfig.tsx:832` `McpConfigView`, rendered at `:768`; `components/ProjectTrustDialog.tsx:175` `ProjectTrustDialogView`, rendered at `:163`; both commented as exported for tests):
  /** The panel for any load and expansion state, without the copy timer; exported for tests. */
  export function SystemPromptPanelView({ loading, prompt, translate, expanded, copied, onCopy, onToggle }: ViewProps)
with `interface ViewProps extends Props { expanded: boolean; copied: boolean; onCopy: () => void; onToggle: () => void }`. `SystemPromptPanel` owns `const [expanded, setExpanded] = useState(false)` and `const [copied, setCopied] = useState(false)`, the copy handler (call `copyText(prompt ?? "")`, `setCopied(true)`, a 1500 ms timeout id kept in a ref, cleared in a `useEffect` cleanup, mirroring `components/MessageView.tsx:412-414` plus the cleanup) and then renders `<SystemPromptPanelView ... />`. Copy always copies the RAW prompt string, never segmented or escaped markdown.
Behaviour (in the view):
1. `const segments = useMemo(() => (prompt ? parseSystemPrompt(prompt) : []), [prompt]);` — the parse lives in this memo so segment strings stay referentially stable and `MarkdownBody`'s own `memo` skips re-parsing on AppShell re-renders.
2. Markup: `<section className={expanded ? "system-prompt-panel is-expanded" : "system-prompt-panel"} aria-label={translate("system.prompt")}>` containing a header `div.system-prompt-header` with `span.system-prompt-title` = `translate("system.prompt")`, then `div.system-prompt-actions` holding exactly two `button type="button" className="system-prompt-button"`: Copy (`{copied ? translate("system.copied") : translate("system.copy")}`, `onClick={onCopy}`, `disabled={!prompt}`) and the toggle (`onClick={onToggle}`, `aria-expanded={expanded}`, `disabled={!prompt}`, label `{expanded ? translate("system.collapse") : translate("system.expand")}`); then the existing `div.system-prompt-scroll`.
3. Inside the scroll area, when `prompt` is truthy render `segments.map(...)`; otherwise render the existing `div.system-prompt-empty` with EXACTLY today's three-way text: `prompt === "" ? translate("system.empty") : loading ? translate("system.loading") : translate("system.load")`.
4. A `section` segment: `<div key={index} className={segment.depth > 0 ? "system-prompt-section is-nested" : "system-prompt-section"} style={{ paddingLeft: Math.min(segment.depth, 3) * 12 }}>` wrapping `div.system-prompt-section-label` with `span.system-prompt-section-name` = `segment.label` and, only when `segment.attributes` is non-empty, `span.system-prompt-section-attributes` = `segment.attributes`.
5. A `prose` segment: `<div key={index} className={segment.depth > 0 ? "system-prompt-segment is-nested" : "system-prompt-segment"} style={{ paddingLeft: Math.min(segment.depth, 3) * 12 }}><MarkdownBody className="system-prompt-body" keepLineBreaks={segment.lineOriented}>{segment.markdown}</MarkdownBody></div>`. `keepLineBreaks` comes ONLY from `segment.lineOriented` — there is no depth condition anywhere in this file (a depth rule put a `<br>` after every hard-wrapped line of the 46 KB AGENTS.md body, which sits at prose depth 2). Preamble prose is depth 0, so it gets neither indent nor border.
6. Keep the inline `<style>{`…`}</style>` block (this panel's convention; do not move CSS into `app/globals.css`). Keep `.system-prompt-panel` (flex column, `height: min(600px, 75dvh)`, `min-height: 220px`, `background: var(--bg-panel)`, `border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border)`), `.system-prompt-scroll` (`min-height: 0; flex: 1; overflow: auto; padding: 12px 16px;`) and `.system-prompt-empty` unchanged; DELETE `.system-prompt-text`. Add:
   .system-prompt-panel.is-expanded { height: min(1200px, calc(100dvh - 160px)); }
   .system-prompt-header { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; padding: 6px 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); flex: 0 0 auto; }
   .system-prompt-title { flex: 1; min-width: 0; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; white-space: nowrap; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text); }
   .system-prompt-actions { display: flex; gap: 6px; flex: 0 0 auto; }
   .system-prompt-button { font: inherit; font-size: 11px; line-height: 1.5; padding: 2px 8px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 6px; background: transparent; color: var(--text-muted); cursor: pointer; }
   .system-prompt-button:hover:not(:disabled) { background: var(--bg-hover); color: var(--text); }
   .system-prompt-button:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 1px; }
   .system-prompt-button:disabled { opacity: .45; cursor: default; }
   .system-prompt-button[aria-expanded="true"] { background: var(--bg-selected); color: var(--text); }
   .system-prompt-section-label { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 10px; margin: 16px 0 6px; }
   .system-prompt-section-label::after { content: ""; flex: 1; height: 1px; background: var(--border); align-self: center; }
   .system-prompt-section-name { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; white-space: nowrap; color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 62%, var(--text-muted)); }
   .system-prompt-section-attributes { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 10px; color: var(--text-dim); white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; max-width: 55%; }
   .system-prompt-section.is-nested, .system-prompt-segment.is-nested { border-left: 1px solid var(--border); }
   .system-prompt-section.is-nested .system-prompt-section-label { margin-top: 10px; }
   .system-prompt-section.is-nested .system-prompt-section-name { font-size: 9px; letter-spacing: .06em; color: var(--text-dim); }
   .system-prompt-panel .system-prompt-body { font-size: 12.5px; line-height: 1.62; }
   Only CSS variables and `color-mix()` (already used across `app/globals.css`); no literal colours; no removed `.markdown-body` rules; no icons/SVG; no height animation.
   Both states stay viewport-relative on purpose: the enclosing popover clamps itself with `maxHeight: calc(100dvh - ${topPanelPos.top}px)` (a `<div style={{ … }}>` at `components/AppShell.tsx:2494-2502`, `maxHeight` at `:2499`, `overflowY: "auto"` at `:2500`) from a MEASURED top, so the panel cannot promise to fit. When the popover is the shorter box IT scrolls; when the panel's content is taller than its own box, `.system-prompt-scroll` scrolls. Do not try to hardcode the popover offset and do not try to force a single inner scroller — the manual check expects one scrollbar, outer or inner.
7. Accessibility: real `<button type="button">` with visible text; the toggle exposes `aria-expanded`; the outer `section` keeps its `aria-label`.

Contract — `components/SystemPromptPanel.test.mjs` (server render, no DOM library exists in this repo): copy the `components/MarkdownBody.test.mjs` harness — `createJiti(import.meta.url, { jsx: { runtime: "automatic" }, tsconfigPaths: true })`, `await jiti.import("./SystemPromptPanel.tsx")`, `await jiti.import("@/hooks/useI18n")` for `I18nProvider` (the bodies render `MarkdownBody`, which needs the provider), `React.createElement` + `renderToStaticMarkup`. Use a RESOLVED-LABEL translate stub so the test can never silently depend on real messages: `const LABELS = { "system.prompt": "System prompt", "system.copy": "Copy", "system.copied": "Copied", "system.expand": "Expand", "system.collapse": "Collapse", "system.empty": "EMPTY", "system.load": "NOT-LOADED", "system.loading": "LOADING" }; const translate = (key) => LABELS[key] ?? `MISSING:${key}`;`. Helper `renderPanel(props)` renders `SystemPromptPanelView` with `expanded: false, copied: false, onCopy() {}, onToggle() {}` defaults. Assert at least:
  1. section labels are real text: for the prompt `<tools>\n- read: Read file contents\n- bash: Run\n</tools>`, the html contains `class="system-prompt-section-name">tools<` and the body is a real list (`<ul>` and `<li>` present) — the regression this feature exists for;
  2. the wrapper tag never leaks: that same html contains neither `<tools` as an element nor the escaped text `&lt;tools`;
  3. header: the title text plus exactly two `<button type="button"` occurrences, both carrying `system-prompt-button`; with `prompt={null}` BOTH are `disabled` and the Copy label is the stub's `Copy`;
  4. `aria-expanded="false"` in the default render; a second render with `expanded: true` yields `aria-expanded="true"`, `system-prompt-panel is-expanded` and the `Collapse` label;
  5. the three empty/loading strings, each via its stub value: `prompt=""` -> `EMPTY`; `prompt={null}, loading: true` -> `LOADING`; `prompt={null}, loading: false` -> `NOT-LOADED`;
  6. no `MISSING:` appears in any rendered html (guards the stub and the key names the panel uses);
  7. `lineOriented` is wired to `keepLineBreaks`: a prompt whose `<skill>` body is `name: pdf` / `description: Read PDFs` / `location: /x/SKILL.md` renders a `<br/>`; a prompt whose body is a hard-wrapped paragraph (`this line is a sentence` / `and this is another line`) renders no `<br/>`.
Steps:
1. Rewrite `components/SystemPromptPanel.tsx`: `"use client"` first line; imports (`useMemo`, `useState`, `useEffect`, `useRef` from `react`, `{ MarkdownBody }` from `"./MarkdownBody"`, `{ parseSystemPrompt }` from `"@/lib/system-prompt-markdown"`, `{ copyText }` from `"@/lib/clipboard"`); `Translate`, `Props`, `ViewProps`; `SystemPromptPanel` (state + copy handler with cleanup) delegating to `SystemPromptPanelView`; the view with the parse memo, header, segment renderers and the verbatim three-way empty branch.
2. Rewrite the inline `<style>` block as listed (keep three rules, delete `.system-prompt-text`, add the rest).
3. Write `components/SystemPromptPanel.test.mjs` with assertions 1-7; run it and fix the component (not the assertions) where they disagree.
Verify: `node --experimental-strip-types --test components/SystemPromptPanel.test.mjs` passes with 0 failures (it also joins `npm test` automatically through the `components/**/*.test.mjs` glob); `npx tsc --noEmit` exits 0; `npx eslint components/SystemPromptPanel.tsx components/SystemPromptPanel.test.mjs` exits 0 (SCOPED to your two files — never run `npm run lint` or `eslint .`, which is red on this tree because of the untracked `.next-old-*` build directory); `grep -n "system-prompt-text" components/SystemPromptPanel.tsx` prints nothing; `grep -nE '#[0-9a-fA-F]{3,6}\b|rgba?\(' components/SystemPromptPanel.tsx` prints nothing; `grep -n "keepLineBreaks" components/SystemPromptPanel.tsx` shows only the `segment.lineOriented` expression; `grep -c "useMemo(" components/SystemPromptPanel.tsx` prints `1`; scope: `git status --porcelain=v1 -- components/SystemPromptPanel.tsx components/SystemPromptPanel.test.mjs` prints exactly two lines, `?? components/SystemPromptPanel.test.mjs` and ` M components/SystemPromptPanel.tsx` (git sorts by path), and you added no other path to the baseline delta (`components/AppShell.tsx`, `components/ChatInput.tsx`, `components/ChatWindow.tsx`, `components/MessageView.tsx`, `components/JsonTree.*` and `components/SystemPromptSelector.tsx` are other work and must stay exactly as the baseline recorded them).
Done when: the panel renders segments through `MarkdownBody` with `keepLineBreaks` bound to `lineOriented`, the empty/loading branch is unchanged word for word, Copy copies the raw prompt, Expand changes only the panel height, the rendered test proves assertions 1-7, and only these two files changed.
